WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:07.899
HBO's Game of Thrones closed out its sixth
season with arguably one of the greatest finales

00:00:07.899 --> 00:00:12.350
in television history...and with one of the
most incredible revelations in the show's

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:16.430
run so far. Oh, and in case you couldn't tell?
Spoilers ahead...

00:00:19.249 --> 00:00:23.720
Bran's vision confirms what fans have long
suspected: Jon isn't actually the bastard

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:29.230
son of Ned Stark. Instead, he's actually Ned's
nephew, the child of his sister Lyanna Stark.

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:32.500
This is huge! And here's why.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:33.810
Half-Targaryen?

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:38.079
We didn't get to fully hear what Lyanna whispered
to Ned just before she died, but it seems

00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:42.539
likely that her baby is the son of Prince
Rhaegar Targaryen. And this handy infographic

00:00:42.539 --> 00:00:46.989
released by HBO a few days after the finale
would seem to confirm this fact.

00:00:46.989 --> 00:00:50.940
Quick refresher: the war that made Robert
Baratheon king in the first place? It started

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:54.739
when Rhaegar apparently abducted Robert's
wife-to-be, Lyanna Stark.

00:00:54.739 --> 00:00:59.320
But Bran's vision revealed that Lyanna gave
birth to baby Jon Snow in the Tower of Joy.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:03.510
We still don't know for sure, but it sure
seems like maybe Rhaegar didn't abduct Lyanna,

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:08.340
but simply invited her to be his lover, and
she willingly accepted. If true, that means

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:13.330
Jon is the son of heirs from two noble houses,
the Starks and the Targaryens. That gives

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:18.390
him a claim to Winterfell and the Iron Throne.
If only Bran can give him the scoop on his

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:19.460
lineage…

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:21.860
Ned Stark's honorable dishonor

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:27.340
Ned Stark had to lie and say that he sired
Jon out of wedlock just to protect Jon's identity.

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:31.930
That brought dishonor to his name and made
his wife, Catelyn, think he'd cheated on her,

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:36.760
all to prevent King Robert from discovering
the infant threat to his new hold on the throne.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:42.130
Ned also forced himself to keep Jon at a distance
to maintain his bastard status, despite him

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:45.970
being the only thing that remained of his
beloved sister. Don't forget Ned's last words

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:48.470
to Jon before he set off for the Night's Watch:

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:56.060
"The Starks have manned the wall for thousands
of years, and you are a Stark. You might not

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:59.140
have my name, but you have my blood."

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:00.570
Thanks, Uncle Ned.

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:02.500
A New Threat to Queen Cersei

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:06.810
We all know the newly-crowned Queen Cersei
is one of the worst villains of the series.

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:10.560
And with no more children left to appoint
as horrible rulers, the likely candidates

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:15.810
to usurp Cersei are Daenerys, Jon, or Petyr
Baelish—but only if he can convince Sansa

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:21.170
Stark to marry him. Nevertheless, Jon unknowingly
has a legitimate claim to the crown, and if

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:25.950
he can prove it, he could march his forces
southward, take the pointy chair, and stop

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.310
the invading White Walkers.

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:30.430
Will he marry Aunt Daenerys?

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:35.620
Being the son of Rhaegar Targaryen makes Jon
Snow Daenerys' nephew. Sorry to everyone hoping

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:41.980
for King Jon to marry the Mother of Dragons
in the end, but that's his auntie. That said...incest

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:46.480
was generally acceptable for the Targaryens.
But if Jaime and Cersei Lannister's twincest

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:50.180
has led to this many problems throughout the
Seven Kingdoms, we don't imagine a happily

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:53.040
ever after love story ending in a shallow
gene pool.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:56.630
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to watch more videos like the one

00:02:56.630 --> 00:03:00.090
you just saw. And leave us a comment to let
us know what you think will happen in Game

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:01.010
of Thrones next...

